in Hollywood films are judged by the  bottom line how much money did they make  how much money did they cost and how  much money did the studio executives get  to pocket but sometimes movies that have  flops at the box office get an  unexpected second life becoming cult  classics as audiences slowly discover  them here's a look at some beloved  movies that totally bombed at the box  office Highlander while today it's  considered one of the best sword &amp;  Sworcery fantasy films of the 80s  Highlander wasn't so well received when  it premiered in 1986 earning a grand  total of twelve point nine million  dollars against a 16 million dollar  production cost once Highlander was  released for the video rental market  though it did much better with viewers  and gained a cult following the fanbase  grew so large that high demand  eventually resulted in the creation of  five sequel films a live-action  television series that ran for six  seasons a series of books and even  comics with a big screen reboot rumored  to be in the works so much for the claim  that there could be only one The  Boondock Saints if it hadn't been for  the now-defunct video rental chain  blockbuster The Boondock Saints never  would have stood a chance showing in  only five theaters in the US the film  meant just four hundred and eleven  thousand dollars worldwide in 1999  despite costing six million dollars to  make then blockbuster stepped in inking  a deal to distribute the film as a  blockbuster exclusive the movie soon  gained a massive cult following bringing  in over fifty million dollars in DVD  blu-ray sales spawning a sequel in 2009  and a new TV series won without stars  Norman Reedus and Sean Patrick Flanery  Scott Pilgrim vs. the world critics  loved Scott Pilgrim vs. the world  calling it funny  heartfelt hilarious vivid and wildly  inventive unfortunately though critics  seem to be the only people who actually  went to the theater to see it as Scott  Pilgrim failed to earn back its  production costs earning less than 48  million dollars worldwide against a  reported 60 million dollar production  budget throw in another twenty five  million dollars spent on advertising  Scott Pilgrim seemed doomed to be a  massive bomb until it sold over 300,000  copies on blu-ray and DVD in its first  week alone Dredd despite a built-in fan  base from the comics and widespread  critical acclaim the 2012 action flick  Dredd earned just 41 million dollars  worldwide which sounds like a lot until  you consider it cost 50  million dollars to make and another 25  million dollars to market part of that  might be lingering bad taste from the  1995 Sylvester Stallone version Judge  Dredd but much of it had to do with bad  timing just a year earlier the cult hit  the raid redemption featured almost the  exact same plot leaving many fans to  consider Dredd a second-rate coffee  judgment whatever the reasons for its  theatrical failure nothing could keep  Dredd down once it hit the home market  where it became an instant success Dredd  sold over 650,000 copies in the first  week it was available on DVD and blu-ray  and by 2017 its total video sale  earnings topped the 20 million dollar  mark leading to rumors of a possible  revival of the franchise The Chronicles  of Riddick  after first appearing in the 2000 film  pitch black vin diesel reprise the role  of Richard B Riddick in the 2004 sci-fi  epic The Chronicles of Riddick with a  budget of 120 million dollars it needed  to be a hit just to break even it wasn't  and it didn't earning just a hundred and  fifteen million dollars worldwide diesel  was even nominated for a Razzie award  for worst actor for his effort  eventually though fans caught on and  slowly turned the Chronicles of Riddick  into a cult hit eventually spawning a  2013 sequel as well as numerous books  action figures and even video games the  Rocky Horror Picture Show it may be the  movie with the longest ever theatrical  run but the Rocky Horror Picture Show  bond during its initial release in 1975  although it was based on a popular stage  musical the film adaptation earned only  twenty one thousand two hundred and  forty five dollars in its opening  weekend the studio yanked the film from  most locations but one exec had a  brilliant idea  why not run it as one of the midnight  shows in the Waverly theater in New York  City literally overnight it became a hit  with the Waverly crowd who just a few  months later turned it into an  interactive experience why shouting  improvised lines at the screen and  singing along the midnight showing soon  spread to other theaters around the  country along with the habit of shouted  audience callbacks eventually dedicated  fans began to form shadow cast  performance troops acting out the film  in costume onstage as the movie plays  out on the big screen behind them within  a year Rocky Horror went from a  box-office bomb to a cult sensation  that's still going strong over 40 years  later  I see you shiver with anticipation  thanks for watching click the looper  icon to subscribe to our YouTube channel  plus check out all this cool stuff we  know you'll love to  [Music]
 

